{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 24, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Hark listen good traveler to thy Japanese sojourn most splendidly penned in rhyme most grand\n\n**First Act Aforethought in Tokyo Where East Doth Meet the West’s Bold Command**\n\nUpon thy arrival in fair Nippon’s gate\nTo Tokyo thou shalt first thy weary feet abate\nIn Shinjuku’s bustle where neon doth gleam\nA thousand tales in lights before thee shall seem\nQuaff sake sweet at Omoide Yokocho’s lane\nWhisper with geisha if fortune doth reign\nThen wander to Shibuya where time stands still\nCrossing scurrying souls in writhing thrill\n\n**Second Day Mount Fuji’s Shadow Doth Beckon Thee**\n\nA train’s swift breath shall bear thee to Hakone’s vale\nWhere hot springs bubble and ryokan dost hail\nDine on kaiseki feast where art doth entwine\nWith nature’s gifts upon thy plate divinely fine\nBehold Fuji’s crown in misty soft repose\nThen bathe in onsen’s warmth where cares may soon dissolve\n\n**Third Scene Kyoto’s Eternal Temples Call Thee Near**\n\nTo Kyoto fair thou must now swiftly repair\nWhere golden pavilions and whispers of samurai are\nAt Fushimi Inari tread paths of red\nThrough torii gates that stretch to heaven’s ledge\nPartake of matcha in a garden serene\nWhere moonlit koi do gently drift unseen\n\n**Fourth Act Nara’s Deer and Ancient Tales Do Lurk**\n\nTo Nara’s ancient halls where time doth lightly stalk\nThou shalt walk with deer in parks of old\nFeed them crumbs and hear their gentle bleat\nThen kneel in Todai-ji’s mighty seat\nWhere Buddha’s gaze doth pierce the soul’s deep core\n\n**Fifth Aforesaid Osaka’s Feasts and Fortunes More**\n\nTo Osaka’s heart where commerce and mirth do thrive\nVisit Dotonbori’s bright and garish drive\nTry takoyaki balls hot from iron’s embrace\nAnd okonomiyaki’s savory grace\nAt Osaka Castle ponder battles fierce and grand\nWhere warriors once did make their fateful stand\n\n**Sixth Day Hiroshima’s Tears and Peace Do Flow**\n\nA solemn train shall bear thee to lands once rent\nWhere shadows linger and the innocent are spent\nAt Peace Park stand and feel the weight of silence\nThen sail to Miyajima where torii rises from the current’s dance\n\n**Seventh Scene Takayama’s Old World Charm Doth Lure**\n\nTo Takayama thou shalt ride on rails of old\nThrough alpine passes where the pines do hold\nTheir ancient secrets in the crisp mountain air\nStroll through morning markets where tradition does fare\n\n**Final Act Return to Tokyo’s Light Where Journey’s End Doth Near**\n\nBack to Tokyo’s glow where fireworks ascendent rise\nAt Sumida River watch the sky ablaze in skies\nLast night a feast at Tsukiji’s bustling port\nWith sushi fresh that doth thy hunger recapture’s worth\n\nFarewell fair traveler from this isle of the gods\nWhere cherry blossoms fall like snowflakes from the sods\nMay thy heart be filled with tales to tell anew\nIn lands afar where thy next adventure’s due.", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.1340528428554535}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.004188099876046181}, {"token": " listen", "logprob": -3.0668089389801025}, {"token": " good", "logprob": -1.205300211906433}, {"token": " travel", "logprob": -0.4940258264541626}, {"token": "er", "logprob": -0.0004456242313608527}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.6352830529212952}, {"token": " thy", "logprob": -1.449173927307129}, {"token": " Japanese", "logprob": -1.6367782354354858}, {"token": " so", "logprob": -0.29126864671707153}, {"token": "journ", "logprob": -0.0012738931691274047}, {"token": " most", "logprob": -1.3822028636932373}, {"token": " splendid", "logprob": -1.5681581497192383}, {"token": "ly", "logprob": -0.4711649417877197}, {"token": " penn", "logprob": -1.2178754806518555}, {"token": "ed", "logprob": -0.0500313937664032}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -1.1423053741455078}, {"token": " rh", "logprob": -2.851223945617676}, {"token": "yme", "logprob": -0.08700135350227356}, {"token": " 